# Motion tokens

Import `motion` from `src/motion/tokens.ts`. Do not inline cubic-bezier arrays or duration literals. New timing = a named token, then consume it.

| Role | Token |
| card / popover enter | `motion.ease.enter` + `duration.enter` (or `popover`) |
| accordion open/close | `motion.ease.standard` + `duration.toggle` |
| finish handoff | `motion.ease.settle` + `duration.settle` |
| chevron | `microTransition()` |
| spinner speed | `motion.spin.deep \| moderate \| intense` |
| speed change | `motion.spin.attack` / `release` |

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
transition={{ duration: 0.25, ease: [0.16, 1, 0.3, 1] }}

// ✅ GOOD
transition={traceTransition({ reduceMotion })}
```

- Reduced motion → `motion.duration.instant`, no spin, no shimmer.
- CSS uses `var(--motion-*)` / `var(--spin-*)` stamped by `applyMotionCssVars()`.
- Origin `--origin-accordion-animation-*` is unused by the trace — do not mix unless migrating on purpose.
